# Line breaks

User pastes a screenshot per band. Lock **those exact wraps**. Do not invent new rag.

Hero, About, Difference, Services, and Process/Calculator desktop are done. Remaining: Navbar, Process/Calculator (tablet/mobile), Reputation, Footer.

## Markup

Three separate copy blocks. Never one block that reflows.

```tsx
<span className="hidden min-[1200px]:!block">
  <span className="block whitespace-nowrap">desktop line 1</span>
</span>
<span className="hidden md:max-[1200px]:!block">
  <span className="block whitespace-nowrap">tablet line 1</span>
</span>
<span className="md:hidden">
  <span className="block whitespace-nowrap">mobile line 1</span>
</span>
```

If a band’s screenshot matches an existing block, keep it — only add nowrap / cqw so it holds across the full band.

## Scale, don’t reflow

Locked nowrap rows that overflow must shrink via `cqw` on `.block`, not wrap. Give the container a definite width (`w-full` or max-width) before using `container-type: inline-size` — nowrap + cqw on a shrink-to-fit parent collapses to 0.

```css
@media (min-width: 768px) and (width < 1200px) {
  .section-copy { container-type: inline-size; }
  .section-copy__tablet > .block {
    font-size: min(1em, calc(100cqw * DESIGN_PX / LONGEST_ROW_PX)) !important;
  }
}
```

Measure `LONGEST_ROW_PX` at the design size for that band.

## Do not

- Do not wrap/stack/move CTAs to “make text bigger”.
- Do not change 821px+ while fixing 768–820 (use `@media (min-width: 768px) and (width < 821px)`).
- Do not use `md:!px-*` on hero/section CTAs if CSS already sets padding — `!` utilities beat later CSS.
- Do not restyle other sections in the same pass.

## New-chat prompt

> Lock line breaks for **[section]** **[mobile | tablet | desktop]** only. Breakpoints: mobile &lt;768, tablet 768–1199 (`md:max-[1200px]`), desktop 1200+. Screenshot is the spec. Do not change button position, layout, or other bands/sections. Hero, About, Difference, Services, and Process/Calculator desktop are already done.
